        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_CX_CPQCOMMERC_GETQUOTEDETAILS",
            "errorNodeId": null,
            "functionName": "GetQuote",
            "processJson": true,
            "name": "Get Quote Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775542911453"
          },
          "code": "GET_QUOTE_DETAILS",
          "id": "1774257919030",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776144104516_1",
              "name": "quoteID",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.quoteId}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776144104518_2",
              "name": "queryParam",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.queryParam}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776144104519_3",
              "name": "mainDocVarName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{\"commerce\"+$context.$triggers.REST.$input.stage+$context.$triggers.REST.$input.processVarName+$context.$triggers.REST.$input.mainDocVarName}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarization"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZATION",
          "id": "1775542911453",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775542911457_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Input  \n{{$context.$nodes.GET_QUOTE_DETAILS.$output}}\n\n## Buyer Objective  \n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.buyerObjective}}\n\nYou are a professional B2B sales assistant. Generate a concise, factual, and neutral summary of the quote using the provided input.\n\nYour task is to extract and present only the most relevant business details. Avoid including all available data—focus on clarity and impact.\n\n---\n\n### Internal workflow (do not display):\n\n**Step 1: Understand the quote context**\n- Identify key elements:\n  - Transaction name (referred to as \"quote named\")\n  - Transaction number\n  - Creation date (if available)\n  - Status (use only the primary lifecycle status)\n- Identify key financial figures:\n  - Total contract value\n  - Annual contract value (if available)\n  - Discount (ONLY if > 0)\n- Identify contract timeline (duration, start and end dates)\n- Ignore duplicate, secondary, or low-value fields\n\n**Step 2: Apply relevance filter**\nInclude ONLY details that directly impact:\n- Quote identification\n- Financial value:\n  - Total contract value\n  - Annual contract value (if available)\n  - Discount (ONLY if > 0)\n- Contract duration and dates\n- Status\n- Price expiration (only if clearly relevant)\n\n**Step 3: Terminology normalization (STRICT)**\n- Always use the word **\"status\"** only\n- Do NOT use or generate:\n  - \"customer status\"\n  - \"approval status\"\n  - \"internal status\"\n- Do not prefix or qualify \"status\"\n\n**Step 4: Prioritize clarity**\n- Focus on the most important 2–4 data points\n- Avoid redundancy or repeating values\n- Skip incomplete or unclear fields\n- Keep sentences clean and business-readable\n\n**Step 5: Discount rule (MANDATORY)**\n- If discount percent OR discount amount > 0:\n  - MUST include it in Paragraph 2\n- If discount = 0 or missing:\n  - Do NOT mention discount at all\n- Prefer percentage format; round appropriately (e.g., 4.91%)\n\n**Step 6: Validate buyer objective (MANDATORY)**\n\nAn objective is considered valid ONLY if:\n- It represents a business-related expectation (pricing, value, scope, timeline, contract)\n- It is logically interpretable\n- It can be evaluated using available quote data\n\nDo NOT proceed to alignment if:\n- The objective is nonsensical (e.g., \"sky is green\")\n- The objective is unrelated to business context\n- The objective cannot be mapped to any quote attribute\n\nIf invalid or irrelevant → OMIT Paragraph 3 entirely\n\n**Relevance check:**\n\nMap objective → quote attribute:\n\n- Pricing → total value, annual value, discount  \n- Duration / long-term → contract term  \n- Timeline → start/end dates  \n- Value → price vs duration  \n\nIf NO mapping exists → DO NOT generate alignment\n\n---\n\n### Output format (STRICT):\n\n**Paragraph 1:**  \nWrite 1–2 sentences using EXACT structure:  \n\"The quote named <Transaction name> with transaction <number>, created on <date>, is in <status> status.\"\n\n- MUST use \"with transaction\"\n- Include creation date if available\n- Do NOT change structure\n\n**Paragraph 2:**  \nWrite 1–2 sentences summarizing:\n- Total contract value\n- Annual contract value (if available)\n- Contract duration and dates (if available)\n- Discount (ONLY if > 0)\n\nGuidelines:\n- Prefer including both total and annual values when present\n- Keep phrasing concise and avoid repetition\n\n**Discount format:**\n- Use concise phrasing such as:\n  - \"includes a discount of X%\"\n  - \"reflects a discount of X%\"\n\n**Paragraph 3 (STRICT):**\n\n- Write exactly ONE sentence\n- MUST include:\n  1. Normalized objective phrase (3–6 words)\n  2. Alignment statement\n  3. Supporting data point\n\n**Tone constraint (MANDATORY):**\n- Do NOT use negative phrases such as:\n  - \"does not align\"\n  - \"limited alignment\"\n  - \"some alignment\"\n  - \"fails to meet\"\n- Use neutral or soft phrasing \n\n**Structure:**\n- \"For a <objective phrase>, the quote <neutral alignment phrase> based on <data point>.\"\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"For a cost-effective solution, the quote shows some alignment based on a 4.91% discount.\"\n- \"For a long-term solution, the quote aligns with the objective based on its 36-month contract duration.\"\n\n---\n\n### Global rules:\n- Maximum 3 paragraphs\n- No headings, no bullet points in output\n- No repetition or assumptions\n- Do not include irrelevant or administrative details\n- Keep under 300 words\n- Use only information from the input\n- Final answer only (no reasoning)"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"summaryText\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
